<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shapsugs</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Shapsugs are a Circassian people of the north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> who lived along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast and the northern slopes of the mountains between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anapa">Anapa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sochi">Sochi</a> area. Among the largest western Circassian communities, they broke the power of their nobles in the late eighteenth century and were governed by assemblies. Most were expelled to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> in 1864; a small community remains near Sochi.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shapsugs.jpg" alt="Shapsugs" width="320" height="121" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yahya Kuadzhe · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shapsug_Banner.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
